{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792490304,"nonce":"eDR/AXlLAfd3F0D5sQZR7tqv0Og=","message":"The command center now mounts its body only after an open request has prepared its mode, picker and carried filter. Closing disposes the command rows/input/footer, clears its local picker and filter, and leaves the small floating-panel shell. Deferred focus callbacks are owned by the mounted body and only run for the matching layout tree. Bound the Command ref and initialize the field before its mode watcher, preserving typed prefixes and line navigation when bodies are recreated.\n\nThe 429-file lifecycle test counts all identities in the tree's registry, including detached floating panels, and all registered Text objects. Both schemes report: closed rows 0, no file enumeration before opening, styled closed 6, styled open 3471, final closed 6. Thus 3465 styled identities exist only while open in this isolated palette fixture. Repeated opens return text and pointer hooks to baseline; command/task/line modes preserve the filter, action selection and line navigation work, and reopening during the close animation restores focus. These are ownership counts, not whole-window footprint or a fixed byte cost per element. No MB savings are inferred from the note's per-element estimate.\n\nPinned Ashui 3cb48b22375465fb8deca217f66bcac68f1eaf82. A fetch of upstream main returned this same revision; no later commit was available at that check. Its InlineFlowRelease regression passes: twenty breadcrumb replacements leave no registered text, and disposing the owner returns Text.byNode to baseline. The image-residency feature remains included.\n\nValidation: scripts/check.sh passes. Command-center lifecycle snapshots and workbench basic/full/production markdownpreview snapshots pass in dark/light, covering actual file/command/task/picker flows and repeated viewport-image release/reentry. Palette and task captures inspected visually. Native bin/rayde rebuilt and RayDE.app refreshed. Logs/captures are bin/palette-*. SNAPSHOT_ONLY=commandcenter scripts/snapshot.sh runs the focused regression.","files":null}]}